  "id": "jr-pokemon-stamp-rally",
  "name": "JR Pokémon Stamp Rally",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Japan Railways companies ran Pokémon stamp rallies for children in the summer holidays from 1997: participants traveled the rail network collecting a different Pokémon stamp at each station, and those who finished won a prize. In several years Pokémon cards came with them: a matte Mew and Surfing Pikachu for finishing JR East's rally in 1997; in 2000, copies of English Wizards of the Coast promos printed in Japan, Eevee and Mewtwo for finishing JR East's courses and, collectors say, Meowth in a pack of goodies sold with JR West's rally pass; and in 2008 Turtwig 117/DP-P, one of the 13 cards of that summer's Collection Challenge, for finishing JR East's, JR Hokkaido's or JR West's rally.",
